Changelog: 05-11-2026 18:44:37

Release 1.2.0.

Changelog: 05-11-2026 12:08:01

Added. The AIC8800D80 of product 0x8820, a UGREEN stick (a69c:5723), takes the legacy-mcu1 branch whatever MCU
it reports, as only that branch supports it (owner, 05-11-2026). legacy-mcu1's loader now prints the chip's
product after its revision; the app reads it and the chip's box shows it ("revision U03, MCU 1, product
0x8820"). The wiki's driver branch says so.

Added. The driver is built from newer commits of shenmintao/aic8800d80 (the Upstream review): main 2e75f88 (was
43db800, 26 commits) and legacy-mcu1 bbf6cb4 (was 1d1b8ff, 24 commits), both of 02-11-2026: fixes for teardown, scans
and network namespaces, Linux 7.3's cfg80211 on legacy-mcu1, and the AIC8800D80 product 0x8820 there. Both still build
with CONFIG_USE_FW_REQUEST off, so the firmware is still read from the folder the app gives as aic_fw_path.

Changelog: 05-11-2026 03:50:19

Release 1.1.2.

Changelog: 05-11-2026 00:15:44

Fixed. The driver did not load any more: SELinux refused the modules (insmod: Permission denied; owner's board,
04-11-2026, Bazzite's image of 26-10-2026 with selinux-policy 44.11 and kernel 7.2.11). Fedora's policy loads a
module only from a file labeled modules_object_t, and the modules under /var/lib/bc250-usb-wifi are var_lib_t. The
service now labels the two modules modules_object_t before it loads them, at every boot, after a rebuild for a new
kernel too. The stick itself was recognized: it waited for the firmware the loader never sent. A service installed
by an earlier version needs Update in the window.

Changelog: 05-11-2026 00:07:05

Fixed. The header's boxes no longer cut their text off (owner, 04-11-2026): Stick, Chip, Driver and Wi-Fi are as
wide as the widest of them, with shorter values (Storage, Waiting, Wi-Fi; the installed branch, with Driver, newest
as the caption for the newest sources), the full text in each box's tooltip. What to do next shows on the right of
the driver's controls, and the explanations of the driver and of the Wi-Fi adapters list are behind a small i.

